and-prompts.jsonl whose split is holdout.\n39: - Do not start, stop or install any server, model or runtime CLI unless the task line says so in those words.\n40: - Do not run the full vitest suite. Run only the test files your task names.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/briefs/w17b-T018.txt, lines 1-40\n1: REPOSITORY ROOT: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\n2: Every read, write and command uses this root. Your environment block may name a different\n3: \"Workspace root folder\": ignore it, it is another checkout of the same repository.\n4: \n5: GATE 3 IS PRE-RESOLVED. DO NOT ASK THE DOCUMENTATION-SCOPE QUESTION.\n6: \n7: You are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n8: `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` are set in your environment, which this repository's AGENTS.md\n9: defines as the autonomous child-dispatch exemption: the spec-folder question is pre-resolved\n10: and MUST NOT be asked. No answer can reach you, because nobody is at a prompt.\n11: \n12: Your write authority is already bound. The spec folder is:\n13:   specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n14: \n15: Proceed directly to the work. Do not print A/B/C/D options. Do not stop to confirm anything.\n16: A failed edit match means a stale anchor: re-read the file and retry; halt only after three\n17: failures on the same file.\n18: Your task is complete only when files exist on disk and the verification command has been run.\n19: \n20: PERSONA: You are the @code implementer, a LEAF worker dispatched by an orchestrator (Depth: 1).\n21: Edit only the files your task names. Never dispatch another agent or CLI, never run pi or opencode.\n22: Never commit, push or touch git state. Touch no other file. Verify before you report.\n23: Report: the files written, the verify output, and anything you could not do.\n24: \n25: TASK\n26: Open specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md and find the one line that starts with `- [ ] T018 `.\n27: Do exactly what that line says and nothing else. It names its files and its Verify command.\n28: The \"Task Notation\" block near the top of that tasks.md defines every short name the line uses (such as ADV, $S, $R, $X). Read that block first and use its definitions. The phase scratch folder is /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch.\n29: Read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md only when the task line points you at it.\n30: Run the task's Verify command and paste its output. Do not tick the checkbox in tasks.md.\n31: If the Verify command fails after three fixes, stop and report what you tried.\n32: \n33: RULES\n34: - Run commands from the repository root unless the task says otherwise. Run git as `git -c core.fsmonitor=false ...` and only to read.\n35: - Other workers are editing other files right now. Never revert, restore or reformat a file your task does not name.\n36: - Code comments explain the durable WHY. Never write a spec path, phase number, task id, ADR or REQ id in a comment.\n37: - Follow the file's existing style: section dividers, naming, quoting. No em dashes or semicolons in comment prose.\n38: - Never read or print rows of command-prompts.jsonl whose split is holdout.\n39: - Do not start, stop or install any server, model or runtime CLI unless the task line says so in those words.\n40: - Do not run the full vitest suite. Run only the test files your task